    "body": "The maintainer confirmed the cause and set the priority, 2026-11-15.\n\nHis words: \"confirmed. the viewport rotataes around the work envelope - not the part.. that is wrong, that is a bug. - issue a fix, P1\"\n\nChanges to this issue:\n\n- Priority is `P1` by the maintainer's word. Effort is `effort:high` (each `P1` is `effort:high` or more).\n- The defect: the camera target is at the centre of the machine work envelope (#1567, `c0b4dfc85`). The orbit must turn about the part.\n\nDone means, in place of the list in the body:\n\n- The work envelope does not move the camera target. The envelope is not part of the bounds that `frame` and the document open use. The target comes from the part and the stock, as before #1567.\n- A test pins the camera target after open and after `frame`, with the envelope display on and off. The two readings are equal.\n- The same check is made for each other display-only body (fixtures and the machine table are named in the PR with the result).\n- The pointer pivot (orbit about the picked point) is not in scope. File a follow-up issue for it.\n",
